Third-party code

The `jev_plays_pokemon/vendor/` directory contains code vendored from other
MIT-licensed open-source projects, which retains its original license terms:

- PyBoy (https://github.com/Baekalfen/PyBoy) — Copyright (c) PyBoy authors, MIT
  License. The intro-navigation logic in `intro.py` is a port of PyBoy's
  `GameWrapperPokemonGen1.start_game`.
- pokemon-agent (https://github.com/NousResearch/pokemon-agent) — Copyright (c)
  Nous Research, MIT License. Vendored: the emulator wrapper, the Red/Blue RAM
  reader, the collision map, and the state builder.
- ClaudePlaysPokemonStarter (https://github.com/davidhershey/ClaudePlaysPokemonStarter) —
  no code vendored; the screen-relative navigation approach in `screen_grid.py`
  is a from-scratch reimplementation inspired by this project.

This project does not distribute any game ROMs, game artwork, or other
copyrighted Nintendo material. You must provide your own legally obtained
copy of the game ROM.